{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 110, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 4 absent, removing edge 5 leaves only edge 0->3 feeding the output, cutting all deep conv paths (e.g. exp 24, a drop of about 16-19 points)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "A strong direct conv on edge 0->3 makes the output less dependent on node 2, so dropping edge 5 hurts less (exp 41 even gained)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the conv on the final edge with a parameter-free skip removes key capacity (exps 57 and 70 dropped 4-12 points)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping the conv on edge 2->3 for pooling removes learned capacity on the main output path (exps 72 and 84)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading a parameter-free direct input-to-output edge to a 3x3 conv adds large capacity (exps 18 and 64 gained 2-10 points)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing pooling on edge 0->3 with a conv gave very large gains (exps 78 and 86), unlike replacing a skip (exps 75 and 85)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip in place of pooling on edge 0->3 helps (exps 23 and 40), whereas a skip in place of a conv hurts badly (exp 92)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing pooling on edge 0->1 with a skip keeps node-1 information intact (exp 14 gained 10-15 points), while 